    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42102" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rŭtŭpĭae</span></b> ,
			ārum, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town and haven of the Cantii</i>,
				<i>in Britain</i>, now <i>Richborough</i>, <i>in Kent.</i>—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Rŭtŭpīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Rutupiœ</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Parent. 18, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc. 6,
					67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					4, 141</span></i>
			.</div>
